course: dictionary
lesson: 8815
title: Words from the farm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sheepdog is a dog that helps a farmer move sheep and look after them. You can work out what a word means from the words around it. «The farmer sent his sheepdog across the hill, and the sheep bunched up and moved toward the gate.» The sheep move because of the dog, so the sheepdog must be the one doing the moving.
explain: Look for clue words. «Sheepdog trials are real competitions where dog and shepherd move sheep through gates and into a pen.» Trials are contests, and the shepherd is the person who works with the dog. Ask yourself: what kind of dog moves sheep? That is the job of a sheepdog.
explain: Some words name a kind of dog. «Border Collie» and «Old English Sheepdog» are breeds, which means particular kinds of dog. A breed is a type, not every dog of that kind. A Border Collie is a breed that is often used as a sheepdog.
fact: A sheepdog is a dog trained to help a farmer move and look after sheep.
fact: A breed is a kind of dog, such as the Border Collie or the Old English Sheepdog, which are often used as sheepdogs.
fact: «Round up» means to gather together, as a sheepdog rounds up sheep by whistle.
fact: «Herding dogs like sheepdogs may nip at running children's heels from instinct.» Instinct means something a dog does naturally, without being taught.
fact: «Sheepdog trials» are competitions where a dog and shepherd move sheep through gates and into a pen.
exercise: «The farmer sent his sheepdog across the hill to bring the sheep home.» What is a sheepdog? | A large cow that lives on a farm | A tractor for moving hay | *A dog trained to help a farmer move and look after sheep
exercise: «Sheepdog trials are real competitions where dog and shepherd move sheep through gates and into a pen.» Find and copy one word that means a contest. | gates | *trials | pen | shepherd
exercise: Ben says a Border Collie is a breed. What does breed mean here? | A whistle used by a farmer | A field where sheep graze | A type of gate | *A kind of dog
test: «The shepherd directs the dog with whistles.» What does directs mean here? | Ignores the dog | *Guides or tells the dog what to do | Feeds the dog | Washes the dog
test: «Herding dogs like sheepdogs may nip at running children's heels from instinct.» What does instinct mean? | A kind of food | Something a dog learns at school | *Something a dog does naturally, without being taught | A loud bark
exam: «The sheepdog rounded up the sheep and brought them through the gate.» What does rounded up mean? | Counted them sleepily | Scattered far apart | Painted them red | *Gathered together
